hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"19172","Waki narrated to us, he said: Shuba narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Abd Allah ibn Rabia al-Sulami, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on a journey and heard a caller to prayer say: I testify there is no god but Allah. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I testify there is no god but Allah. He said: I testify Muhammad is Allah's Messenger. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I testify I am Muhammad the Messenger of Allah. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You will find him a shepherd of sheep or away from his family. Then when he descended the valley he said: He passed a discarded kid and said: Do you see this worthless to its folk? The world is more worthless to Allah than this is to its folk."
